WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.900
This field guide introduces an organization's r2c-tracker administration page and the setup process for a new site administrator.

00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:17.600
It covers account activation, privacy and retention, service status, usage oversight, member roles, device enrollment, and flight records.

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:22.700
Use demonstration information during training and keep real credentials and invitation links private.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:32.000
The r2c-tracker platform administrator creates the organization and identifies its primary site administrator.

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:36.600
The administrator receives an activation email at the approved organization address.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:38.600
Open the invitation promptly.

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:42.800
Activation links are single-use and normally expire after seven days.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:50.900
If the name, organization designator, or email address is wrong, stop and contact the platform administrator before activating.

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:58.000
The activation page displays the organization designator and the exact invited email address.

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:04.000
Continue with that Google account, or create an r2c-tracker password of at least 12 characters.

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:09.600
Activation confirms that you are authorized to enable the organization's account in the open-ended beta.

00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:15.000
During beta testing, each organization receives a generous platform-funded usage allowance.

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:26.100
After activation, sign in at r2c-tracker.com, slash, your organization designator.

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:29.500
The organization directory can also take you there.

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:32.800
Use the same approved Google identity or your R2C password.

00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:42.900
The administration page shows the organization name, designator, and signed-in administrator so you can verify that you are working in the correct tenant before making changes.

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:47.600
Begin with privacy and retention.

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:58.400
The organization owner chooses whether flight records are restricted to authenticated users or publicly visible, sets the notification email, and defines retention periods for flight records and raw logs.

00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:01.000
Restricted visibility is the safer default.

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:08.100
These are organization-owned policies, and the platform administrator cannot view the organization's flight records or logs.

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:16.900
The service status panel shows the organization's beta status, provisioning, usage allowance, and attributed usage.

00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:21.000
R2C tracker does not accept payments during beta testing.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:26.000
Organization owners and billing administrators should review usage before and during an operational period.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:35.900
Then decide who receives the video requester role and coordinate when streaming is appropriate for the team's priorities and available allowance.

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:39.000
Use members and delegated roles to add approved personnel.

00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:41.900
Enter the member's name and exact email address.

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:44.400
Then grant only the roles required for the job.

00:02:44.500 --> 00:02:47.500
Billing administrators monitor usage and service status.

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:51.100
User administrators manage members and enrollment campaigns.

00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:54.500
Records administrators manage flight records.

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:56.400
Records viewers have read access,

00:02:56.500 --> 00:03:00.200
and video requesters may request pilot-authorized streams.

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:04.500
Pending members activate by signing in with the exact invited Google address.

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:10.100
Create an enrollment campaign when RID2Caltopo field devices need organization access.

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:13.800
Give the campaign a clear operational label.

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:18.100
Choose a short validity period and limit the number of device enrollments.

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:23.500
The resulting QR code contains a signed, expiring, and revocable enrollment capability.

00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:31.100
It does not contain administrator passwords, FAA credentials, or an unrestricted tracker upload secret.

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:36.200
Revoke the campaign when distribution is complete or if the code may have escaped your control.

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:42.000
Organization owners and records administrators can open Flight Records and Migration.

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:51.500
Use it to review incident and training flights, export organization records, import a legacy archive, or backfill weather and metadata from a CSV.

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:55.500
Treat exports as organization records.

00:03:55.600 --> 00:04:01.400
Store them according to policy, and verify the organization and date range before importing or sharing them.

00:04:02.500 --> 00:04:09.500
The administration page controls who can manage the organization, but field authority stays with the field team.

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:20.400
Site administrators decide who receives the video requester role and should coordinate when streaming serves the operation and fits the team's available allowance.

00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:27.500
A requester may ask to view an active stream, but video does not leave the field device until the pilot approves that request in RID2Caltopo.

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:31.800
Review roles before each operational period and remove access that is no longer needed.

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:37.700
Before the first operation, confirm the organization identity and notification email.

00:04:37.900 --> 00:04:44.500
Review privacy and retention. Check beta status, allowance usage, and recent activity.

00:04:44.500 --> 00:04:51.384
Add named members with least-privilege roles and give the video requester role only to people responsible for coordinating streams.

00:04:51.384 --> 00:04:54.800
Create a short-lived enrollment campaign for the correct devices,

00:04:55.200 --> 00:05:00.300
then revoke it when enrollment is complete. Finally, verify that flight record and video

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:06.600
access match your organization's policy. Your r2c-tracker site is now ready for controlled field use.

